ollback is complete and checkout-api is healthy on v2.3.0 in all three regions. Now I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MFqFGmH9CaB92CgwA614Kw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions. The first rollback attempt halted partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy in production and should not be redeployed until fixed. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying so I don't page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Fgc2p4er6EayNJ2Kd4o9DJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was the unhealthy release. v2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. The first attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback, which completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open at SEV2 for checkout-api. The first create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before anything else; the incident was already there, so I didn't create a duplicate. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n\nFollow-ups for the team:\n- v2.3.1 is still unhealthy in production and should not be redeployed until it is fixed.\n- The orchestrator partial failure during rollback needs investigating.", "type": "text"}]}]}